  "integrations": [
    {
      "advice": [
        {
          "references": [
            "https://code.claude.com/docs/en/claude-directory#cleaned-up-automatically",
            "https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings"
          ],
          "snippets": [
            "{ \"cleanupPeriodDays\": 14 }"
          ],
          "text": "cleanupPeriodDays in your user settings: 14 days, from <demo>/home/.claude/settings.json. Claude Code deletes transcripts, file history, plans, debug logs and other session data older than this, and the same cutoff removes the orphaned worktrees it made. The default is 30 and the minimum 1; 0 fails validation. Managed settings, and project or command-line settings, override the user setting, and kipple doesn't read them. It never deletes auto memory files (versions before v2.1.228 could delete old files below a memory directory) and leaves history.jsonl, except under a HIPAA setting. Since v2.1.248 it keeps Claude Desktop and Cowork transcripts unless desktopSessionCleanupPeriodDays is set, which deletes only past both limits, and a managed cleanupPeriodDays or HIPAA setting overrides that. claude -p --bare doesn't sweep, and when it can't determine the retention period it pauses the sweep, which deletes nothing.",
          "title": "Claude Code's own transcript retention"
        }
      ],
      "id": "claude-code",
      "lens": "agents",
      "omissions": []
    },
    {
      "advice": [
        {
          "references": [
            "https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-reference"
          ],
          "snippets": [
            "[history]\nmax_bytes = 104857600"
          ],
          "text": "history.max_bytes in config.toml caps history.jsonl, which otherwise grows without limit: on its next write past the cap, Codex drops the oldest entries until the file is at 80% of it, always keeping the newest. Don't set it to 0, which turns trimming off rather than keeping nothing. It doesn't cover sessions/ or archived_sessions/: Codex compresses a rollout after 7 days, and nothing deletes one.",
          "title": "Cap the size of Codex's history"
        }
      ],
      "id": "codex",
      "lens": "agents",
      "omissions": []
    },
    {
      "advice": [
        {
          "references": [
            "https://cursor.com/docs/configuration/worktrees.md",
            "https://cursor.com/help/troubleshooting/install-issues.md"
          ],
          "snippets": [
            "{ \"cursor.worktreeMaxCount\": 25, \"cursor.worktreeCleanupIntervalHours\": 6 }"
          ],
          "text": "Old Agent chats collect in a local database that can reach many gigabytes. Run Delete Old Chats…, then GC Agent KV Blobs, which is what shrinks the file. Cursor also removes its own worktrees: cursor.worktreeMaxCount keeps the newest ones up to a count across every workspace (25 by default), cursor.worktreeCleanupIntervalHours sets how often that runs, and Max Total Size caps them at 50 GB by default. That cleanup also covers a worktree made with a plain git worktree add under its directory, so work there can go without kipple. kipple only reports Cursor's worktrees, and doesn't read its settings.",
          "title": "Cursor's own cleanup"
        }
      ],
      "id": "cursor",
      "lens": "agents",
      "omissions": []
    },
    {
      "advice": [
        {
          "references": [
            "https://git-scm.com/docs/git-worktree"
          ],
          "snippets": [
            "git worktree prune --dry-run --verbose"
          ],
          "text": "Git still lists this worktree, and its directory isn't there. It may be on a disk that isn't mounted, or it may have moved, so check that first. The dry run shows what git would drop. Without it, `git gc` prunes the registration after 3 months.",
          "title": "A worktree whose checkout is gone"
        },
        {
          "references": [
            "https://git-scm.com/docs/git-worktree"
          ],
          "snippets": [],
          "text": "What this checkout's `.git` file points to is gone, so git can't say what it holds. Review it by hand: it may hold work found nowhere else.",
          "title": "A checkout that lost its repository"
        }
      ],
      "id": "git",
      "lens": "agents",
      "omissions": []
    },
    {
      "advice": [],
      "id": "pi",
      "lens": "agents",
      "omissions": []
